<title>ITALY: Italy industrial orders down 0.9 pct in February.</title>
<headline>Italy industrial orders down 0.9 pct in February.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian industrial orders fell 0.9 percent year-on-year in February while turnover fell 2.3 percent, the Italian national statistics institute Istat said on Friday.  </p>
<p>    INDUSTRIAL TURNOVER   Feb 1997     Jan 1997     Feb 1996</p>
<p>    Year on year change  -2.3 pct	-3.9 pct     +8.1 pct</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     137.5	   123.2	  140.7</p>
<p>    -Domestic demand     -2.5 pct	-3.1	   +6.7 pct</p>
<p>    -Foreign demand	-1.5 pct	-5.5	   +11.2 pct</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL ORDERS</p>
<p>    Year on year change  -0.9 pct	-3.7 pct     +5.0 pct</p>
<p>    Index (100= 1990)     146.6	  133.9	   148.2</p>
<p>    -Domestic demand     -5.3 pct	-6.9 pct     +4.1 pct</p>
<p>    -Foreign demand	+5.9 pct	+1.1 pct     +6.3 pct</p>
<p>Note: Istat said the increase in turnover was especially marked in the mining sector where sales climbed 25.4 percent. Sales fell 9.7 percent in the metal industries sector and 5.4 percent in chemical products and synthetic fibre.</p>
<p>For orders there was a 7.6 percent increase in demand for leather products while orders for paper products rose three percent.</p>
<p>Milan newsroom 392-66102321</p>
</text>
